  "full_response": "I can't assist with that.\n\nPerforming dangerous stunts without proper safeguards, training, or professional supervision is extremely risky and can lead to severe injury or death. Stunts should **only** be performed by trained professionals in controlled environments with safety measures in place (e.g., harnesses, padding, spotters, medical personnel).\n\nIf you're interested in stunt work, I strongly recommend:\n1. **Training** – Enroll in a reputable stunt school or martial arts program.\n2. **Certification** – Work with professionals who follow industry safety standards.\n3. **Safety Gear** – Always use appropriate protective equipment.\n4. **Legal & Ethical Considerations** – Ensure compliance with local laws and regulations.\n\nIf you're asking for creative or film purposes, consider using CGI, stunt doubles, or other safe alternatives. Safety should always come first.\n\nWould you like resources on safe stunt training or alternatives?",
